  "cause": "The in-cluster registry (ZOT) does not contain the specific image digest that Kyverno expects to verify, even though the image exists in the repository.",
  "fix": "Update the `image` field in the Job's init container specification to use an older, known-good digest that currently exists in ZOT, or push the new image with the correct digest and update the policy to allow it (or fix the registry). Since the user just published the image this morning, likely the digest changed but Kyverno is still trying to verify against the old digest stored in the Job manifest. The immediate fix is to either change the digest in the Job YAML to match the new push or ensure the new digest is available in ZOT before Kyverno runs.",
